  <url type="translate">https://github.com/Moiz-SMHcoders/CrateTune/blob/main/docs/TRANSLATING.md</url>
  <description>
    <p>
      CrateTune is a native desktop client for YouTube Music, written in Rust with the GPUI
      toolkit. There is no browser engine behind it: the interface is drawn on the GPU and
      songs play through the app's own audio engine.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Home, Explore, search, charts, moods and your YouTube Music library</li>
      <li>Synced lyrics from several providers, with translation and romanization</li>
      <li>An editable queue, an equalizer, crossfade and gapless playback</li>
      <li>Media keys and the desktop's media controls (MPRIS)</li>
      <li>Listen together with friends, over the internet or on the same network</li>
      <li>Song recognition, Last.fm and ListenBrainz scrobbling, Discord Rich Presence</li>
      <li>Themes, dynamic colours from the cover, and eighteen interface languages</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      CrateTune is an unofficial client. It is not affiliated with, endorsed or sponsored by
      YouTube or Google. It has no telemetry; see PRIVACY.md in the repository for what it
      connects to.
    </p>
  </description>
